# =================================================================
# SECTION 1: THE AMENDING STATUTE
# =================================================================

lld:XIV-413 a llo:Statute ;
    rdfs:label "Amendment to Cybersecurity Law – Vulnerability Disclosure and EU Certification (No. XIV-413)" ;
    rdfs:label "Amendment to Cybersecurity Law – Vulnerability Disclosure and EU Certification (No. XIV-413)"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Kibernetinio saugumo įstatymo Nr. XII-1428 1, 2, 6, 8, 9, 13 straipsnių, V skyriaus pavadinimo, priedo pakeitimo ir įstatymo papildymo 17 straipsniu ir VI skyriumi įstatymas (Nr. XIV-413)"@lt ;
    rdfs:comment "Introduces two major new regimes into the Cybersecurity Law: (1) a coordinated vulnerability disclosure framework (Article 17) with safe harbour protections for security researchers, 24-hour reporting deadlines, 90-day coordinated disclosure timelines, and researcher conduct restrictions; (2) national cybersecurity certification authority powers (new Chapter VI, Articles 18-20) designating NKSC as the national authority under EU Cybersecurity Act Regulation (EU) 2019/881, with investigation, enforcement, and conformity assessment body supervision powers. Also adds the 'vulnerability' definition, expands NKSC powers to include vulnerability analysis and binding orders, redefines KSIS as a state information system with confidentiality rules, and updates the EU annex to include Regulation (EU) 2019/881." ;
    rdfs:comment "Introduces two major new regimes into the Cybersecurity Law: (1) a coordinated vulnerability disclosure framework (Article 17) with safe harbour protections for security researchers, 24-hour reporting deadlines, 90-day coordinated disclosure timelines, and researcher conduct restrictions; (2) national cybersecurity certification authority powers (new Chapter VI, Articles 18-20) designating NKSC as the national authority under EU Cybersecurity Act Regulation (EU) 2019/881, with investigation, enforcement, and conformity assessment body supervision powers. Also adds the 'vulnerability' definition, expands NKSC powers to include vulnerability analysis and binding orders, redefines KSIS as a state information system with confidentiality rules, and updates the EU annex to include Regulation (EU) 2019/881."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Įveda du naujus pagrindinius režimus į Kibernetinio saugumo įstatymą: (1) koordinuoto spragų atskleidimo sistemą (17 straipsnis) su saugumo tyrinėtojų apsauga, 24 valandų pranešimo terminais, 90 dienų koordinuoto atskleidimo terminais ir tyrinėtojų veiklos apribojimais; (2) nacionalinės kibernetinio saugumo sertifikavimo institucijos įgaliojimus (naujas VI skyrius, 18-20 straipsniai), paskiriančius NKSC nacionaline institucija pagal ES Kibernetinio saugumo aktą – Reglamentą (ES) 2019/881, su tyrimo, vykdymo užtikrinimo ir atitikties vertinimo įstaigų priežiūros įgaliojimais. Taip pat prideda 'spragos' sąvoką, išplečia NKSC įgaliojimus apimant spragų analizę ir privalomus nurodymus, apibrėžia KSIS kaip valstybės informacinę sistemą su konfidencialumo taisyklėmis ir atnaujina ES priedą, įtraukiant Reglamentą (ES) 2019/881."@lt ;
    llo:hasDocID "No. XIV-413" ;
    llo:dateEnacted "2021-06-17"^^xsd:date ;
    llo:isPubliclyDisclosed true ;
    llo:proposesAmendmentTo lld:XII-1428 ;
    llo:hasComponent lld:XIV-413_Art1 ,
                     lld:XIV-413_Art2 ,
                     lld:XIV-413_Art3 ,
                     lld:XIV-413_Art4 ,
                     lld:XIV-413_Art5 ,
                     lld:XIV-413_Art6 ,
                     lld:XIV-413_Art7 ,
                     lld:XIV-413_Art8 ,
                     lld:XIV-413_Art9 ,
                     lld:XIV-413_Art10 ,
                     lld:XIV-413_Art11 .


